---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
	title="Contact Us — Daisy's Dailies"
	description="Get in touch with the Daisy's Dailies team — bug reports, feature requests, and account help."
	heading="Contact"
	kicker="Support"
>
	<h1>Contact Us</h1>
	<p>
		We'd love to hear from you! Whether you have a question, found a bug, or have a
		suggestion to make Daisy's Dailies even better, don't hesitate to reach out.
	</p>

	<h2>Get in Touch</h2>

	<Callout tone="important">
		<p><strong>Sibert Strategy Group</strong></p>
		<p>Email: <a href="mailto:daisysdailies@sibertstrategygroup.com">daisysdailies@sibertstrategygroup.com</a></p>
		<a
			href="mailto:daisysdailies@sibertstrategygroup.com"
			class="btn btn-primary mt-3 no-underline"
		>
			Send Us an Email
		</a>
	</Callout>

	<h2>What We Can Help With</h2>

	<Callout tone="info">
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Bug Reports</strong> — Something not working as expected? Let us know and we'll look into it.</li>
			<li><strong>Feature Requests</strong> — Have an idea that would make the app better? We're all ears.</li>
			<li><strong>Account Issues</strong> — Trouble signing in, managing your subscription, or deleting your account.</li>
			<li><strong>General Questions</strong> — Anything else about Daisy's Dailies.</li>
		</ul>
	</Callout>

	<h2>Response Time</h2>

	<p>We typically respond within 24–48 hours. To help us assist you faster, please include:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Your device type (iPhone, Android, tablet)</li>
		<li>A description of the issue or question</li>
		<li>Any screenshots that might help illustrate the problem</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>In-App Support</h2>

	<p>
		You can also contact us directly from within the app by going to 
		<strong>Settings → Contact Us</strong>. This automatically includes your device and
		app version info, which helps us troubleshoot faster.
	</p>

	<hr />

	<p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
		See also our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> and
		<a href="/terms-of-service">Terms of Service</a>.
	</p>
</LegalLayout>
